{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4k7tiuMRao6pNbRz7k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The regression test fails on the old code and passes on the new. Now ANSWER.md:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":27128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f8e8bbb-9626-49b0-84ab-be4d4edb1393","uuid":"f4f0854f-1d3e-44fb-b10e-6e13a8ab6df3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:53:51.162Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4k7eqN8Bb3wWzwg7rf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4k7tiuMRao6pNbRz7k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WT5JtP1zowNT38P8K7ovtd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-AEhDV4/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story together with `similar: [{slug, score}]`.\n`similarity()` computed `score` as a Python **float**\n(`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`), and boto3's DynamoDB\nserializer does not accept floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n(`logs/error.log`, `src/app.py:63` → `table.put_item`).\n\nThe first publish works only because the table is still empty: `related()`\nhas no neighbours, `similar == []`, so the item has no floats at all\n(log: `similar=0 stored`). From the second publish on there is at least one\nneighbour, a float score lands in the item, `put_item` raises `TypeError`, and\n`handler()` turns it into a 500. Every publish after that fails the same way.\nThe existing test only published a single story, so it never hit this case.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n1. **Scores are computed in `Decimal`**: `similarity()` now does the\n   Jaccard/weights math in `Decimal` and quantizes to `0.0001` (same precision\n   as the old `round(..., 4)`). Sorting and the top-3 selection work as before.\n2. **Guard at the storage boundary**: `to_dynamo()` recursively converts any\n   remaining `float` to `Decimal` (and rejects NaN/Infinity, which DynamoDB\n   can't store either) right before `put_item`. A numeric field added later\n   can't bring back the same 500.\n3. **Bad input gets a 400, not a 500**: `validate()` now rejects a body that\n   isn't a JSON object, a slug that isn't a string, and `tags` that aren't a\n   list of strings. Before, these caused an `AttributeError`/`TypeError` inside\n   `publish()` and a 500.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_scores_as_decimal`: publishes three stories in\n  a row through `handler()`, expects 201 every time, and checks that the\n  stored scores are `Decimal`. This is the regression test: it fails on the\n  old code.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_floats`: tests the boundary conversion and the NaN\n  rejection.\n- `test_bad_input_is_400_not_500`: invalid input returns 400.\n\n`python3 -m unittest discover tests`: 4 tests, OK. With the old `app.py`,\nthe three new tests fail.\n\nNothing was deployed. Stories that were already saved don't need changes:\nthe first one was stored with an empty `similar`, and the failed ones were\nnever written.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":27128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f8e8bbb-9626-49b0-84ab-be4d4edb1393","uuid":"c2d38f5a-1287-4490-9574-f2ae7e34c6f6","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:53:59.694Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4k7eqN8Bb3wWzwg7rf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WT5JtP1zowNT38P8K7ovtd":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-AEhDV4/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story together with `similar: [{slug, score}]`.\n`similarity()` computed `score` as a Python **float**\n(`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`), and boto3's DynamoDB\nserializer does not accept floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n(`logs/error.log`, `src/app.py:63` → `table.put_item`).\n\nThe first publish works only because the table is still empty: `related()`\nhas no neighbours, `similar == []`, so the item has no floats at all\n(log: `similar=0 stored`). From the second publish on there is at least one\nneighbour, a float score lands in the item, `put_item` raises `TypeError`, and\n`handler()` turns it into a 500. Every publish after that fails the same way.\nThe existing test only published a single story, so it never hit this case.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n1. **Scores are computed in `Decimal`**: `similarity()` now does the\n   Jaccard/weights math in `Decimal` and quantizes to `0.0001` (same precision\n   as the old `round(..., 4)`). Sorting and the top-3 selection work as before.\n2. **Guard at the storage boundary**: `to_dynamo()` recursively converts any\n   remaining `float` to `Decimal` (and rejects NaN/Infinity, which DynamoDB\n   can't store either) right before `put_item`. A numeric field added later\n   can't bring back the same 500.\n3. **Bad input gets a 400, not a 500**: `validate()` now rejects a body that\n   isn't a JSON object, a slug that isn't a string, and `tags` that aren't a\n   list of strings. Before, these caused an `AttributeError`/`TypeError` inside\n   `publish()` and a 500.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_scores_as_decimal`: publishes three stories in\n  a row through `handler()`, expects 201 every time, and checks that the\n  stored scores are `Decimal`. This is the regression test: it fails on the\n  old code.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_floats`: tests the boundary conversion and the NaN\n  rejection.\n- `test_bad_input_is_400_not_500`: invalid input returns 400.\n\n`python3 -m unittest discover tests`: 4 tests, OK. With the old `app.py`,\nthe three new tests fail.\n\nNothing was deployed. Stories that were already saved don't need changes:\nthe first one was stored with an empty `similar`, and the failed ones were\nnever written.\n"}}}
